valid_prefix = records[:-1]\\n            else:\\n                valid_prefix = []\\n    if valid:\\n        return {'valid': True, 'records': records}\\n    else:\\n        return {'valid': False, 'records': records, 'violation': {'line': violation_line, 'valid_prefix': valid_prefix}}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to parse the problem: implement `solve(case)` that returns a JSON-serializable object. The task is given as \"AGENT-RA-01\" with registry_id \"B\". The fixture shows cases with a list of \"lines\" strings. The description mentions parsing interleaved Thought, Action, Observation, Final records. We need to validate the sequence according to ReAct trajectory rules.\n\nRules inferred from description:\n- Each non-terminal cycle: Thought, then Action, then Observation. \n- Final only at the end and only at a reasoning boundary.\n- On first violation, return one-based line and valid prefix.\n- Return lowercase typed trajectory records and an explicit validity flag.\n- Need to parse each line: \"Thought: ...\", \"Action: ...\", \"Observation: ...\", \"Final: ...\". Also \"Action Input\" maybe? The description mentions \"Action Input\" but in examples only \"Action: lookup\" etc. Might need to handle \"Action Input\" as separate? But the fixture lines only have \"Thought:\", \"Action:\", \"Observation:\", \"Final:\". So we will parse those prefixes.\n\nWe need to return something like: \n{\n  \"valid\": boolean,\n  \"records\": list of dicts with \"type\" (lowercase: thought, action, observation, final) and \"text\" (the content after colon),\n  \"violation\": optional dict with \"line\" (1-based) and \"valid_prefix\" (list of records up to violation? Or maybe string? The description says \"return its one-based line and the valid prefix.\" The valid prefix likely is the list of records up to the violation. But need to output JSON-serializable. Probably a dict with \"line\" and \"valid_prefix\" as list of records (or maybe the lines?).\n}\n\nBut we must loo